]\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In addition to changing the value of an individual element, you can also","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change the values of a slice of elements in a mutable collection. For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example, you can sort ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"part"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" of a mutable collection by calling the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"mutable ","type":"text"},{"code":"sort()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" method on a subscripted subsequence. Here’s an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"example that sorts the first half of an array of integers:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var numbers = [15, 40, 10, 30, 60, 25, 5, 100]","numbers[0..<4].sort()","print(numbers)","\/\/ Prints \"[10, 15, 30, 40, 60, 25, 5, 100]\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"MutableCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol allows changing the values of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collection’s elements but not the length of the collection itself. For","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"operations that require adding or removing elements, see the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"RangeReplaceableCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol instead.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Conforming to the MutableCollection Protocol","level":1,"anchor":"Conforming-to-the-MutableCollection-Protocol"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"To add conformance to the ","type":"text"},{"code":"MutableCollection","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" protocol to your own","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"custom collection, upgrade your type’s subscript to support both read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and write access.","type"